      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Case 1 is a 57-year-old man with pelvic recurrence 1 year 8 months after surgery for ascending colon cancer.We performed a Hartmann's operation.He has been relapse-free for 11 years.Case 2 is a 67-year-old man with intraperitoneal small intestinal relapse 4 years after surgery for cecum cancer.We performed resection.He has brain metastases recurrence in 2 years 6 months after surgery, died after 2 years 9 months.Case 3 is a 53-year-old man with recurrence in the bladder rectal fossa 5 years after sigmoidectomy.We performed resection.He has been relapse-free survival at 1 year 2 months."},
